{
  "dom_id": "step-q68888",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Jordan did an experiment in his Chemistry class. He heated a liquid whose initial temperature was $-{1.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ After several minutes, the temperature of the liquid increased by ${7.3}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$, at which point he decided to end the experiment. What was the final temperature of the liquid?",
  "worked_solution": "To determine the final temperature of the liquid, we add the variation in temperature to the initial temperature of the liquid. This gives\n\n$$\n-{1.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}+{7.3}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}={6.1}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the temperature of the liquid at the end of the experiment was ${6.1}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
